;Other Territories
*{{flag|Australia}}. [[Ashmore and Cartier Islands]] - Special authorisation required.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.environment.gov.au/resource/ashmore-reef-and-cartier-island-marine-reserves-information-visitors |title=Ashmore Reef and Cartier Island Marine Reserves - Information for Visitors |access-date=4 August 2017}}</ref>
*{{flag|Colombia}}. [[San Andrés Island|San Andrés]] and [[Leticia, Amazonas|Leticia]] - Visitors arriving at [[Gustavo Rojas Pinilla International Airport]] and [[Alfredo Vásquez Cobo International Airport]] must buy tourist cards on arrival.
*{{flag|Crimea}} - Visa issued by Russia is required.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.themoscowtimes.com/news/article/foreigners-now-need-russian-visa-to-visit-crimea/497173.html|title=Foreigners Now Need Russian Visa to Visit Crimea|date=April 2014 }}</ref>
*{{flag|Ecuador}}. [[File:Bandera Província Galápagos.svg|border|22x20px]] [[Galapagos Province|Galápagos]] - Online pre-registration is required. Transit Control Card must also be obtained at the airport prior to departure.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://gobiernogalapagos.gob.ec/cgggob/info/|title=INFORMACIÓN A LA CIUDADANÍA – Consejo de Gobierno de Regimen Especial de Galápagos|website=gobiernogalapagos.gob.ec|access-date=2017-06-29|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150221022358/http://gobiernogalapagos.gob.ec/cgggob/info/|archive-date=2015-02-21}}</ref>
*{{flag|Eritrea}} outside [[Asmara]] - To travel in the rest of the country, a Travel Permit for Foreigners is required (20 [[Eritrean nakfa]]).<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.eritrea.be/MoT.htm|title=Ministry of Tourism - Tourism Service Center|first=Hans van der|last=Splinter|website=www.eritrea.be}}</ref>
*{{flag|Fiji}}. [[Lau Province]] - Special permission required.<ref>{{cite web|title=Fiji Country Specific Information|url=http://www.travel.state.gov/travel/cis_pa_tw/cis/cis_1114.html#entry_requirements|publisher=Bureau of Consular Affairs, U.S. Department of State|access-date=18 November 2013|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131102204202/http://travel.state.gov/travel/cis_pa_tw/cis/cis_1114.html#entry_requirements|archive-date=2 November 2013|df=dmy-all}}</ref>
*{{flagicon|Greece}} [[File:Flag of the Greek Orthodox Church.svg|21px]] [[Mount Athos]] - Special permit required (4 days: 25 [[euro]] for [[Eastern Orthodox Church|Orthodox]] visitors, 35 euro for non-Orthodox visitors, 18 euro for students). There is a visitors' quota: maximum 100 [[Eastern Orthodox Church|Orthodox]] and 10 non-Orthodox per day and women are not allowed.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.athosfriends.org/PilgrimsGuide/planning/|title=The Friends of Mount Athos - A Pilgrim's Guide to Mount Athos: Planning Your Visit|website=www.athosfriends.org|access-date=23 December 2013|archive-date=1 December 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171201154734/http://athosfriends.org/PilgrimsGuide/planning/}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.mountathosinfos.gr/pages/agionoros/pilgrims_info.en.html|title=Mount Athos Infos . gr|date=1 December 2007|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20071201150655/http://www.mountathosinfos.gr/pages/agionoros/pilgrims_info.en.html|archive-date=2007-12-01}}</ref>
*{{flag|India}}. Prior approval from the [[Ministry of Home Affairs (India)|MHA]] required for whole of [[Arunachal Pradesh]], [[Nagaland]], [[Manipur]], [[Mizoram]] and [[Sikkim]] and parts of states [[Uttaranchal]], [[Jammu and Kashmir (union territory)|Jammu and Kashmir]], [[Rajasthan]], [[Himachal Pradesh]]. Restricted Area Permit (RAP) required for all of [[Andaman and Nicobar Islands]] and parts of [[Sikkim]]. Some of these requirements are occasionally lifted for a year.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.timaticweb.com/cgi-bin/tim_website_client.cgi?FullText=1&COUNTRY=IN&SECTION=VI&SUBSECTION=00&user=KLMB2C&subuser=KLMB2C |title=Visa information |access-date=2013-12-17}}{{dead link|date=May 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://as.and.nic.in/TourismAND/TCorner/ForeignersNew.htm |title=Entry Formalities to Andaman |access-date=26 November 2013 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120426085021/http://as.and.nic.in/TourismAND/TCorner/ForeignersNew.htm |archive-date=26 April 2012 }}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://arunachaltourism.com/entry_formalities.php |title=Arunachal Tourism |access-date=1 August 2014 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140701111837/http://arunachaltourism.com/entry_formalities.php |archive-date=1 July 2014 }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=http://lakshadweeptourism.nic.in/web9.htm |title=Tourism in Lakshadweep |access-date=2014-08-01 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140713171604/http://lakshadweeptourism.nic.in/web9.htm |archive-date=2014-07-13 }}</ref>
*{{flag|Iran}}. [[Kish Island]] - Visa not required.<ref>{{cite web|title=Iran Country Specific Information |url=http://www.travel.state.gov/travel/cis_pa_tw/cis/cis_1142.html#entry_requirements |publisher=Bureau of Consular Affairs, U.S. Department of State |access-date=18 November 2013 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131203094257/http://www.travel.state.gov/travel/cis_pa_tw/cis/cis_1142.html |archive-date=3 December 2013 }}</ref>
*{{flag|Kazakhstan}}. Closed cities - Special permission required for the town of [[Baikonur]] and surrounding areas in [[Kyzylorda Oblast]], and the town of [[Gvardeyskiy, Kazakhstan|Gvardeyskiy]] near [[Almaty]].<ref>{{cite web | title=Kazakhstan Country Specific Information | url=http://www.travel.state.gov/travel/cis_pa_tw/cis/cis_1150.html#entry_requirements | publisher=Bureau of Consular Affairs, U.S. Department of State | access-date=18 November 2013 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131102170930/http://travel.state.gov/travel/cis_pa_tw/cis/cis_1150.html | archive-date=2 November 2013}}</ref>
*{{Flag|Kurdistan Region}}. You can apply for an e-Visa (30 days) to visit the Iraqi Kurdistan Region.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://visit.gov.krd | title=Iraqi Kurdistan e-Visa}}</ref>
*{{flag|Malaysia}}. {{flagicon|Sabah}} [[Sabah]] and {{flagicon|Sarawak}} [[Sarawak]] - Malaysian Visa / eNTRI required. These states have their own immigration authorities but same visa policies applies as West Malaysia. However a single entry Visa / eNTRI is valid for multiple entry/exit between the territories inside Malaysia.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://cs.mfa.gov.cn/zggmcg/ljmdd/yz_645708/mlxy_647012/ | title=马来西亚-入境居留 | website=中国领事服务网}}</ref>
*{{flag|Maldives}} outside [[Malé]] - Permission required. Tourists are generally prohibited from visiting non-resort islands without the express permission of the Government of Maldives.<ref>{{cite web|title=Maldives Country Specific Information |url=http://www.travel.state.gov/travel/cis_pa_tw/cis/cis_961.html#entry_requirements |publisher=Bureau of Consular Affairs, U.S. Department of State |access-date=18 November 2013 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131202232123/http://www.travel.state.gov/travel/cis_pa_tw/cis/cis_961.html |archive-date=2 December 2013}}
</ref>
*{{flag|North Korea}} outside [[Pyongyang]] - Special permit required. People are not allowed to leave the capital city, tourists can only leave the capital with a governmental tourist guide (no independent moving).
*{{flag|Russia}} - Several [[Russian closed city|closed cities and regions in Russia]] require special authorization.<ref>{{cite web|title=Russian Federation Country Specific Information|url=http://www.travel.state.gov/travel/cis_pa_tw/cis/cis_1006.html#entry_requirements|publisher=Bureau of Consular Affairs, U.S. Department of State|access-date=18 November 2013|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131203003453/http://www.travel.state.gov/travel/cis_pa_tw/cis/cis_1006.html#entry_requirements|archive-date=3 December 2013|df=dmy-all}}</ref>
*{{flagicon|Saudi Arabia}} [[Mecca]] and [[Medina]] - Special access required. Non-Muslims and those following the [[Ahmadiyya]] religious movement are strictly prohibited from entry.
