==Hong Kong, Macau and Taiwan==
===Hong Kong and Macau SARs===
* Rather than passports, Chinese citizens from mainland China may travel to Hong Kong and Macau with an in-lieu travel document named [[Exit-Entry Permit for Travelling to and from Hong Kong and Macau]] (EEP-HKMO) to align with the position that Hong Kong and Macau are Chinese territories rather than foreign. EEP holders must apply for an endorsement which serves as both the exit permission from mainland China and the de facto entry ticket for Hong Kong or Macau. EEP holders without an endorsement shall be prohibited from departing from mainland China. It is the [[National Immigration Administration|Immigration in mainland China]] rather than that in Hong Kong and Macau that is responsible for issuing endorsements.<ref name=immd>{{cite web|url=https://www.immd.gov.hk/eng/services/visas/overseas-chinese-entry-arrangement.html|title=Entry Arrangements for Mainland, Macao, Taiwan & Overseas Chinese Residents}}</ref>
* Chinese passport holders intending to transit via Hong Kong or Macao between mainland China and a foreign third place may travel directly with their Chinese passport without applying for EEP and an endorsement. They are eligible for stay up to 7 days without a (de facto) entry ticket.<ref name=immd/>
* Chinese passport holders residing abroad on a long-term basis may apply for a {{interlanguage link|sticker-style HKSAR entry permit|lt=|zh|中华人民共和国香港特别行政区进入许可}} at Chinese missions abroad. The sticker shall allow up to (1) two entries within three months, 30 days stay for each entry; or (2) multiple entries within two years, 14 days stay for each entry.<ref>{{cite web |title=中国香港签证/进入许可_中华人民共和国驻新加坡共和国大使馆 |url=http://sg.china-embassy.gov.cn/lsfw/fhqz/xgamqz/201706/t20170620_1925142.htm |website=sg.china-embassy.gov.cn}}</ref> There is no similar sticker for Macao. Instead, they can enter Macao for 7 days (extendable to 90 days) if they possess a document showing that they reside abroad on a long-term basis.<ref>{{cite web |title=境外中国公民前往港澳 |url=http://sydney.china-consulate.gov.cn/lszj_122929/qz/jwzggmqwga/202204/t20220429_10675493.htm |website=sydney.china-consulate.gov.cn |publisher=Consulate-General of the People's Republic of China in Sydney |access-date=13 June 2025}}</ref>

