==Exit and Entry Permit==
[[File:Personal Info Page People's Republic of China Entry and Exit Permit for Border Tourism Only.png|thumb|A sample of the personal info page of the Entry and Exit Permit for Border Tourism]]

In addition to passports, Exit and Entry Permit were issued to citizens of the People's Republic of China for visiting certain land neighboring countries for trade, tourism purposes without a passport, and visa to the country of visiting and vice versa under the bilateral agreements.<ref name=gab>{{cite web | language=zh|title=公安部出入境管理局负责人就贯彻落实《护照法》答记者问 | publisher=中华人民共和国公安部 | date=2006-06-01 | url=http://www.mps.gov.cn/n16/n1237/n1342/127806.html | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131219172802/http://www.mps.gov.cn/n16/n1237/n1342/127806.html | archive-date=2013-12-19 | access-date=2013-12-19}}</ref><br /> Such permit is issued by the police stations in the related border administrative divisions. By far, travelers from the administrative divisions that share borders with [[North Korea]], [[Mongolia]], [[Myanmar]], [[Laos]], [[Vietnam]], [[India]] and [[Nepal]] could apply for the Exit-Entry Permit for crossing borders.<ref>{{cite news | title=边境地区出入境通行证核发服务指南 | url=https://www.nia.gov.cn/n741445/n741604/n741673/c815619/content.html | publisher=国家移民管理局 | date=2019-06-18 | language=zh | archive-date=17 July 2021 | access-date=15 July 2021 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210717195659/https://www.nia.gov.cn/n741445/n741604/n741673/c815619/content.html }}</ref>

